    "datasource": "Kodak Professional Supra 100, 400 and 800 Color Negative Films, publication E-2519, May 2003; SHA256 878a0075415ed294ec0d0c32fc336ee43dbfb5aad0c4b50605d9514e3dc4242c. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-supra-100/recipe.json. Dye spectra: kodak_portra_400 shapes, scaled so their mixture reproduces this sheet's own midscale-neutral-minus-D-min. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Measured, not assumed: the sheet's D-min trace is the spectral base density, and what the Status M densitometer reads through it is subtracted from the characteristic curves. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_portra_400. The same stock whose dye shapes this sheet is prepared with; a Kodak C-41 colour negative. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9008, 1.0758, 0.869], log-exposure shift [-0.243, 0.0, -0.274], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 45.4% before, 14.5% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
